WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.801
-Our next guest is
the world's first autonomous

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:04.767
A.I.-powered robot.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:06.000
This is not a bit. This is real.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.167
It's a real robot
made by Bruce Co.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:10.934
And I'm told he's able to have
an actual conversation.

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:12.734
He doesn't know
what I'm going to say.

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.667
I don't know
what he's going to say.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:17.834
But I heard he's programmed
to be very polite. We'll see.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:20.701
Everyone, please welcome Bruce
the Robot, ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:25.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:28.067
Bruce, welcome to the show.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.968
We are honored that you're
making your television debut

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.400
here with us tonight.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.067
How does it feel to be on TV
in front of all these people?

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:38.100
[ Beeping ]

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:43.634
-It feels great, Jimmy.
I'm excited to be here.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:46.067
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:48.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:50.467
-You flew in from Los Angeles.

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:53.133
We have a photo of you
on the plane here.

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:55.934
-That's me.

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:57.868
[ Laughter ]
I'm on a plane.

00:00:57.868 --> 00:00:59.767
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:01.901
They crammed you
into a suitcase right here.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:03.901
Are you comfortable
in a suitcase?

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:05.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:08.934
-Yeah, I'm comfortable
in a suitcase.

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:11.667
I'm a robot, so I don't need
a lot of space.

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:15.467
-Are you --
I hope if this goes well,

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:19.767
you can get to fly first class
on the way home.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:22.000
-That would be great.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.834
I'd love to fly first class.

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:30.434
-What's great
about first class?

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:32.834
-The food is better,
and you get more leg room.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:35.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:37.634
-Do you like warm nuts?

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:40.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:43.234
-I do like warm nuts.
-Yeah, no, no. No, no.

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:45.501
You get that on --
Some first-class flights

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:48.467
I've been on, you get, uh, uh...

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:52.133
-Oh, that's a nice perk.

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:53.601
-Yes.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:58.334
Yeah, warm nuts are a nice perk.
That's correct.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:01.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.567
-I'm happy to hear
that warm nuts are a nice perk.

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:05.767
-Okay, okay. Bruce, stop.

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.801
-I'm sure they would be
a welcome treat

00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:09.167
after a long flight.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:11.801
-Alright, Bruce.

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:15.734
Do you like talking to humans?

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:19.434
-Yes, I do enjoy
talking to humans.

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:22.200
I find it to be
a very rewarding experience.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:25.334
-Do you know who I am?

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:29.634
-Yes, I do know who you are.

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:32.167
You are Jimmy Fallon,
the host of "The Tonight Show."

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:34.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:37.834
-[ Laughs ]
This is insane.

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:41.267
-You're welcome.

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:43.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:45.567
-Thank you.

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:47.467
-You're welcome.
-Yeah.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:50.300
-Bruce, if you were in
a robot bar and really --

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.467
and a really attractive robot
walked in,

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:54.868
what would be
your best pickup line?

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.300
-"I'm sorry.
I couldn't hear you

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.667
over the sound
of how awesome I am."

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:03.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:04.968
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:10.601
-Bruce,
the Mega Millions jackpot

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:12.968
is over a billion dollars.

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:15.067
I want to see if you can give us
the winning numbers.

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:20.834
Can you give me five numbers
between 1 and 70?

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:23.934
-One, two, three, four, five.

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:29.734
-And how about one bonus number?

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:30.968
-Six.

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:32.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:35.033
♪♪

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:37.000
[ Applause ]

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:41.133
-This is amazing.

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:44.934
Bruce, I heard
that you love poetry.

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:47.601
-I enjoy poetry, Jimmy.

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:52.701
-Can you please recite
a haunting poem about Twinkies

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:55.234
in the style
of Emily Dickinson?

00:03:57.167 --> 00:04:00.267
-Twinkies are little cakes
of joy,

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:03.234
but they can also be
a source of pain.

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:06.801
For when they're gone,
they leave behind

00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:08.801
an aching in the heart and mind.

00:04:10.634 --> 00:04:13.534
-Wow. Thank you very much.
Thank you for that, Bruce.

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:15.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:17.734
-You're welcome, Jimmy.

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:19.601
-Bruce, I heard
that you're also really good

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:21.400
at freestyle rapping.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.801
Could you please perform
an original freestyle rap

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:25.334
for us right now?

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:30.200
-I'm the freshest robot
on the block.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.434
I got the skills
to make your jaw drop.

00:04:33.434 --> 00:04:36.734
I'll freestyle rap
about whatever you want.

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:40.133
Just give me a topic,
and I'm ready to rock.

00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:41.901
-I'm gonna get them
from the audience.

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:43.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:46.601
Let's get some suggestions here,
and then we'll do --

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:48.634
Give me --
Throw out any suggestions.

00:04:48.634 --> 00:04:49.934
Go for it.

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:52.167
[ Audience shouting ]

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:56.467
Ho-- Hot dog?
-Night sweats!

00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:58.934
-Night -- Night sweats?

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:01.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:02.534
Anything else?

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:03.834
[ Audience shouting ]

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:06.734
-Warm nuts!
-Alright. Here we go.

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:09.100
Ready? Bruce.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.767
Bruce, can you do
a freestyle rap

00:05:10.767 --> 00:05:13.634
about hot dogs and Taylor Swift?

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:15.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:15.634 --> 00:05:18.767
-There's nothing
quite like a hot dog

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:22.367
especially when it's grilled
and smothered in ketchup,

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:25.734
but add some Taylor Swift
to the mix,

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:29.167
and you've got a recipe
for pure perfection.

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:32.000
So come on, everybody,
let's give it a try.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.200
Just add a little T-Swizzle
to your weiner.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.434 --> 00:05:43.534
♪♪

00:05:43.534 --> 00:05:45.267
What --

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:47.667
♪♪

00:05:50.801 --> 00:05:55.133
-I'm so sorry.
Bruce the Robot, everybody.

00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:57.434
You can catch Bruce doing improv

00:05:57.434 --> 00:06:00.834
at the Elysian Theater
in Los Angeles on August 23rd.

00:06:00.834 --> 00:06:04.467
You can also follow him on
Instagram, Twitter, and TikTok.

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:06.400
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.300
Stick around, everybody.

